 "text": "Hi, how's your day been so far? Lovely. Lots of energy. A long lunch rather than shorter afternoon so the parents can join in is best for a napping toddler. Cutting them gives better texture for little fingers to grip. Pack them in small bags or boxes instead of bowls. Blend big themes like treasure hunts, den building or spot the differences games with little direction. Kids love the surprise. A shaded spot is crucial, even on hot days. A blanket to lie on can save your back. Yes, potty training snacks and drinks. A few spare blankets and toys in case the rain comes.",
